fix:
Replace the domain record with a named struct and migrate index-based consumers to named fields. Introduce distinct field types as well where compile-time prevention of same-representation swaps is needed; field names alone clarify meaning but do not make such swaps impossible.
```rust
struct Address {
    street: String,
    city: String,
    state: String,
    zip_code: String,
}

struct Rectangle {
    width: f64,
    height: f64,
}

fn calculate_area(rect: &Rectangle) -> f64 {
    rect.width * rect.height
}
```
